values ('e3f4a5b6-7c8d-4e33-8a23-3b4c5d6e7f33', 'theater-history-i', 'Theater History I', 'This course surveys theater and performance from ancient Mediterranean traditions through the 18th century, while training students to think like theater historians. Students study plays, performance spaces, actors, audiences, institutions, technologies, and archival traces across Western and selected global traditions. The course emphasizes how theater history is constructed, whose performances are preserved, and how historical knowledge can inform contemporary theater practice.');

